  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Trump Exchange**: Any player with the 7 or 2 of trumps can swap it for the face-up 'Life' card if the Life card is a point card (A, 3, K, Q, J). 2. **Cooperation**: The two opponents may peek at each other's hands throughout the game but are forbidden from verbal signaling. 3. **The Trick**: Play is counter-clockwise. Each opponent plays ONE card. The Alcalde then plays TWO cards. 4. **No Follow Suit**: Players can play any card; they are not required to follow the suit of the lead. 5. **Winning Tricks**: The highest trump wins. If no trumps, the highest card of the led suit wins. 6. **Drawing**: After a trick, the winner draws (2 cards for Alcalde, 1 for opponents) followed by others in order.",
    Player: "1. **Trump Exchange**: Any player with the 7 or 2 of trumps can swap it for the face-up 'Life' card if the Life card is a point card (A, 3, K, Q, J). 2. **Cooperation**: The two opponents may peek at each other's hands throughout the game but are forbidden from verbal signaling. 3. **The Trick**: Play is counter-clockwise. Each opponent plays ONE card. The Alcalde then plays TWO cards. 4. **No Follow Suit**: Players can play any card; they are not required to follow the suit of the lead. 5. **Winning Tricks**: The highest trump wins. If no trumps, the highest card of the led suit wins. 6. **Drawing**: After a trick, the winner draws (2 cards for Alcalde, 1 for opponents) followed by others in order.",
    objective: 'As Alcalde: Score 60+ points to retain the title. As Opponents: Prevent the Alcalde from reaching 60 points to depose them.',
    gameplay: "1. **Trump Exchange**: Any player with the 7 or 2 of trumps can swap it for the face-up 'Life' card if the Life card is a point card (A, 3, K, Q, J). 2. **Cooperation**: The two opponents may peek at each other's hands throughout the game but are forbidden from verbal signaling. 3. **The Trick**: Play is counter-clockwise. Each opponent plays ONE card. The Alcalde then plays TWO cards. 4. **No Follow Suit**: Players can play any card; they are not required to follow the suit of the lead. 5. **Winning Tricks**: The highest trump wins. If no trumps, the highest card of the led suit wins. 6. **Drawing**: After a trick, the winner draws (2 cards for Alcalde, 1 for opponents) followed by others in order.",
    keyRules: [
      "Alcalde plays twice per trick, meaning they control the final 'slap' of the round.",
      'Point Values: Ace=11, 3=10, King=4, Queen=3, Jack=2. Total in deck = 120 points.',
      "The 'Life' card is drawn as the very last card of the deck.",
      'If the Alcalde fails to reach 60, the player to their right becomes the new Alcalde for the next hand.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
